          {
            "sourceIndex": 0,
            "text": "Bring the heavy whipping cream to a boil. Pour it on the chocolate, wait a few seconds then mix well until the mixture is homogeneous.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19378"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 1,
            "text": "Beat the softened butter and sugar together.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19377"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 2,
            "text": "Beat in the egg. Mix.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19376"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 3,
            "text": "Then, add the almond flour and mix well.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19377"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 4,
            "text": "Add the melted chocolate to the almond preparation and mix well. If this preparation is too thin (because it is still hot), leave to cool in the refrigerator for 10-15 minutes.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19379"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 5,
            "text": "Roll out one sheet of puff pastry. Spread the chocolate-almond filling over the center of the dough, leaving a 1 inch (1.2 cm) exposed border. If you wish, place a little porcelain figurine \"fève\" in the filling.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19380"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 6,
            "text": "Brush the edges of the pastry with water and cover with another circle of dough on top and press down to seal the edges.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19381"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 7,
            "text": "If you want, with a knife or just with your fingers, decorate the edges.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19382"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 8,
            "text": "Brush with beaten yolk. Place in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19419"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 9,
            "text": "Preheat oven to 390F (190C).",
            "mediaId": null
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 10,
            "text": "Brush with yolk one more time. Using a knife, create a design on top of your galette. Poke 3-5 holes, to allow steam to escape while baking.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19384"
          },
          {
            "sourceIndex": 11,
            "text": "Bake for 30 minutes or until the pastry is golden brown.",
            "mediaId": "wordpress-attachment:19397"
          }
        ]
